FIRST SCHEDULE
Regulation 7 (c) (i)
Particulars required to be contained in returns of births under regulations 3, 5, 6 and 7.
1. Ship in which birth occurred —
(a)name of the ship; and
(b)official number.
2. Child —
(a)date and time (in Greenwich Mean Time) of birth;
(b)
(i)if the birth takes place at sea, the position of the ship by latitude and longitude at the time of birth; and
(ii)in any other case, the place of birth;
(c)name (if any) and surname; and
(d)sex.
3. Father —
(a)name and surname;
(b)country of domicile;
(c)race and nationality;
(d)National registration identity card or passport number;
(e)occupation, rank or profession; and
(f)date of birth,
but if the child is illegitimate, no particulars of the father shall be given except at the joint request of the mother and of the person acknowledging himself to be the father, given to the informant in writing and signed by both the mother and that person.
4. Mother —
(a)name;
(b)
(i)maiden surname; and
(ii)surname at marriage, if different from maiden surname;
(c)country of domicile;
(d)race and nationality;
(e)National registration identity card or passport number; and
(f)date of birth.
5. Informant —
(a)full name of master;
(b)country of domicile;
(c)race and nationality;
(d)address; and
(e)qualification.

SECOND SCHEDULE
Regulation 7 (c) (ii)
Particulars required to be contained in returns of deaths under regulations 4, 5, 6 and 7.
1. The ship in which the death occurred or in which the deceased was employed —
(a)name of ship;
(b)official number; and
(c)name of its owner and his address.
2. The deceased —
(a)date of death or loss;
(b)
(i)if the death takes place on board the ship or in a ship’s boat or if the deceased is lost from the ship or a ship’s boat, the place of death or, if at sea the position of the ship or ship’s boat by latitude and longitude at the time of death or loss (as the case may require); and
(ii)in any other case, the place of death;
(c)name and surname;
(d)sex;
(e)date of birth (if known) or age;
(f)maiden surname (if known) in case of a married woman;
(g)occupation, rank or profession;
(h)usual residence at time of death or loss;
(i)race and nationality;
(j)National registration identity card or passport number; and
(k)cause of death or loss (certified if possible by the ship’s doctor or other medical practitioner).
3. Informant —
(a)full name of master;
(b)country of domicile;
(c)race and nationality;
(d)address; and
(e)qualification.
